# Copy to ~/.config/terva-lampi/agent.env (mode 0600).
# The systemd user unit reads this file when it exists. A value here
# wins over config.json and loses to a command-line flag. Leave both
# unset and config.json decides, then the loopback default and
# ~/.config/terva-lampi/token. `terva-lampi status` prints which layer
# won as source=flag, env, config, or default.
#
# Phase 0 places the lake on a small VPS (docs/policy.md). Set
# LAMPI_SERVER to that host's HTTPS URL, here or as server in
# config.json. The loopback value is for a local terva-lampi serve.
# Do not invent a hostname in git, and do not point the agent at plain
# HTTP on a public interface.

# LAMPI_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:8787
# LAMPI_TOKEN_FILE=/home/you/.config/terva-lampi/token
#
# Harness enable and root belong in
# ~/.config/terva-lampi/config.json. See deploy/config.json.example.
# Restart the user unit after editing that file. The agent reads it
# at start. A harness environment variable is a debug override and
# loses to a config root. Precedence is flag (if any), then config
# root, then env, then the adapter default. No per-harness root flag
# exists. Do not put a production hostname or a token in this file.
